    {
      "datasource": {"type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana"},
      "description": "The baseline drives measured BFD and convergence runs. The candidate adds service dual-homing for deterministic N-1 and shared-risk audits.",
      "gridPos": {"h": 12, "w": 14, "x": 0, "y": 6},
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "code": {"language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false},
        "content": "### OSPF Area 0 · measured baseline\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060text\n                      SERVICE  10.20.0.0/24\n                               │ cost 10\n                    ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n                    │       core1         │\n                    └──────────┬──────────┘\n                               │ cost 20\n                    ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n                    │       core2         │\n                    └─────────────────────┘\n\n             PRIMARY  ━━━ cost 10     BACKUP  ┄┄┄ cost 100\n\n     core1 ━━━ agg1 ━━━ access1      core1 ┄┄┄ agg2 ┄┄┄ access1\n     core2 ━━━ agg2 ━━━ access2      core2 ┄┄┄ agg1 ┄┄┄ access2\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n**access1 normal** \u0060access1 → agg1 → core1 → service\u0060 · **metric 30**  \n**tested failover** \u0060access1 → agg2 → core2 → core1 → service\u0060 · **metric 140**\n\n---\n\n**Audit candidate** keeps this fabric and adds \u0060core2 → service-host\u0060 at cost \u006030\u0060 for service dual-homing. It is used by the modeled N-1/SRLG audits, not by the measured BFD trial.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.0",
      "title": "TOPOLOGY & PATH POLICY",
      "type": "text"
    },
