        "code": {"language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false},
        "content": "### How to read the evidence\n\n**Measured sequence** \u0060carrier-up blackhole → BFD Down → OSPF Neighbor Down → route metric 30 → 140 → ICMP recovery\u0060  \nLive offsets come from the collector's monotonic clock with 100 ms polling, so they are **observed upper bounds**. Prometheus scrapes every 1 second for visualization only. Results apply to this local containerlab topology and configuration—not to a production SLA.  \n**Audit boundary** N-1 proves modeled reachability. It does not prove physical path diversity, capacity headroom, or an availability target.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.0",
      "title": "MEASUREMENT CONTRACT",
      "type": "text"
